The top 5, distilled

1. Electrical CoC (Voltguard) — legally mandated, deadline buyer, registration moat
2. Solar/inverter maintenance contracts — recurring revenue on existing installed base
3. Estate CCTV / access maintenance — estate contracts, recurring, physically moated
4. Essential repair and maintenance — non-discretionary, low capital
5. Electrical and property maintenance coordination — layered on #1 and #4

The bottom line

Of 76 models, only the top 3–5 have a structural reason to exist that isn't "I'll outwork the competition."

The other 70 are all variations of:

· Commoditised services (bookkeeping, VAs, cold email, review generation)
· Capital-heavy trades (manufacturing, importing, restaurants)
· Credential-gated professions (medical, legal, financial)
· Software/product plays (SaaS, apps, marketplaces — wrong model for a solo non-technical founder)
· Cash bridges (niche websites, appointment setting)

Voltguard ranks #1 because it's the only one where the law does your selling for you. That's the whole ranking. Everything below it is a harder version of the same game.
